                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "530e2613-f860-44ed-9753-0fff138b29c8",
                        "entry_id": "8a213208-4be1-3a30-a33e-87d1673ee228",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most atomy"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                        "entry_id": "8a213208-4be1-3a30-a33e-87d1673ee228",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a tiny particle; made up of tiny particles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d126ba7-b2ed-4510-b90b-50213ca4ffcb",
                                "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                                "text": "[…] noble Lesser Alps which were clothed in rich velvety green all the way up and had little atomy Swiss homes perched upon grassy benches along their mist-dimmed heights."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "24a21b1b-67f4-45d2-9e16-40080ef2d04c",
                                "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                                "text": "1894, Richard Henry Savage, The Princess of Alaska, Chicago and New York: Rand, McNally, Book 2, Chapter 8, p. 235,\n[…] the atomy speck, hurled through space, which we mortals call the world!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a91fb4e9-6531-4c1a-91a2-cba95f27b575",
                                "sense_id": "bb7c6709-5c3c-33f8-ae1e-85c411998efd",
                                "text": "Things that flit in the sky or creep\nIn the atomy dust, or swarm in the deep,"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                "word": "atomy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a5a19ba3-97bf-4734-bcce-50acfc505f3c",
                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "atomy"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "97378644-7b30-4de1-94fd-280ceb30cf90",
                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "atomies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A floating mote or speck of dust."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "548c5e59-243d-45d9-893e-01b86244fb9b",
                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                "text": "And thicker then in sunne are Atomies,\nFlew bullets, fier, and slaughtered dead mens cries."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5141033-c49c-419c-87b1-82210661569c",
                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                "text": "That eyes, that are the frail’st and softest things\nWho shut their coward gates on atomies\nShould be call’d tyrants, butchers, murderers!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d94471a-8175-4e3c-9c0e-280a45361a2e",
                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                "text": "Thinke not that all betwixt the Wherpoole, and the Sprat,\nI goe about to name, that were to take in hand,\nThe Atomy to tell, or to cast vp the sand;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a56f912-1a69-4742-8f8b-e96d0246527b",
                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                "text": "[…] the crew\nSeemed in that light, like atomies to dance\nWithin a sunbeam;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0335ef64-98e6-40c3-a010-3b50b1feb864",
                                "sense_id": "8af7cc51-e4cf-36a4-b392-d980b4bc506f",
                                "text": "1880, Richard Francis Burton, The Kasidah, London: H. S. Nichols, 1894, p. 7,\nThe marvel is that man can smile dreaming his ghostly ghastly dream;—\nBetter the heedless atomy that buzzes in the morning beam!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An indivisible particle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4a4937d-ea0e-41b0-a613-f25b1a7a783d",
                                "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                                "text": "Lastly, it [an Element] is the least part or Atomie of that thing which is made, or proceedeth from it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fe26a45-ab11-4e4d-be73-b4480bc8d593",
                                "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                                "text": "And freely men confesse that this world’s spent,\nWhen in the Planets, and the firmament\nThey seeke so many new; they see that this\nIs crumbled out againe to his Atomies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6493403c-ea29-4c14-8b77-3a5815a1840b",
                                "sense_id": "29ebf343-f7e4-3c49-809e-6ead894de60c",
                                "text": "[…] praise thy God,\nO be not selfe-conceited, least his rod\nDoe bruise thee into Atomies;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                        "entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tiny being; a very small person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a46956a2-b123-4eb3-a66e-5303e90cd711",
                                "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                                "text": "[…] she [Queen Mab] comes\nIn shape no bigger than an agate-stone\nOn the fore-finger of an alderman,\nDrawn with a team of little atomies\nAthwart men’s noses as they lie asleep;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "955f5573-4c15-4930-afeb-9fff5ece5584",
                                "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                                "text": "Was there a \"delicate atomy\" of minute dimensions and pale complexion, he forthwith strutted a hardy Highlander."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cbf0031-7067-4a17-9582-d23d061d30c1",
                                "sense_id": "a4051275-a41f-3880-be57-1b171328cb43",
                                "text": "“Hey!” he said, “why, it’s Tom! I suppose you have come here to laugh at me, you spiteful little atomy?”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "350a01d3-96e6-48e4-bcca-59c979d2906d",
                        "source_entry_id": "dd62db25-c6ee-37ae-95c8-386e82b7c7b4",
